{# CATERING band (theme.components.catering; needs client.catering filled).

   For a client whose catering is a real second business rather than a
   marketing line — it gets a band of its own, on ink, between the
   reservation band and visit. The action is whatever client.catering.ctaHref
   says: a mailto to the catering kitchen, a tel:, or the party-inquiry page.

   Two photographs at different scales rather than a pair: the first is the
   subject and runs tall, the second is a smaller supporting frame offset
   below it. Equal twins read as a gallery; unequal ones read as a
   photograph with a footnote. Both are in flow — the offset is a margin on
   the second frame, not padding on a shared wrapper, because an absolutely
   positioned child resolves against the padding box and an intended overlap
   becomes a collision.

   Ink, and no pattern. The build this came from ran it on the brand's deep
   clay under a Japanese wave-scale at 4%, and the pair read as talavera —
   a texture composes with the ground it sits on, so test it there. The
   warmth stays in the accent on the eyebrow and button, and the photographs.

   A step deeper than secondary-700 so it does not flatten into a
   menus_schedule band or the footer. #}
<section id="catering" class="ground-ink relative isolate section overflow-hidden bg-secondary-800">
  <div class="container-site">
    <div class="grid grid-cols-1 items-center gap-14 sm:gap-24 lg:grid-cols-12 lg:gap-16">

      {# Centred while stacked, left once the copy sits beside the
         photographs at lg — the same rule about_seam and menus_schedule
         follow. #}
      <div class="text-center lg:col-span-5 lg:text-left" data-reveal="up">
        {% if client.catering.eyebrow %}<p class="eyebrow">{{ client.catering.eyebrow }}</p>{% endif %}
        <h2 class="section-title !mt-3 text-white lg:after:mx-0">{{ client.catering.title or "Catering" }}</h2>
        {% if client.catering.lede %}<p class="mt-6 text-pretty text-lg/8 text-gray-300">{{ client.catering.lede }}</p>{% endif %}
        {% if client.catering.ctaLabel %}
        <a
          href="{{ client.catering.ctaHref }}"
          class="btn-accent mt-9 block w-full rounded-btn border border-transparent px-7 py-3.5 text-center text-sm font-semibold uppercase tracking-[0.08em] sm:inline-block sm:w-auto"
        >{{ client.catering.ctaLabel }}</a>
        {% endif %}
        {% if client.catering.ctaNote %}<p class="mt-4 text-sm text-gray-400">{{ client.catering.ctaNote }}</p>{% endif %}
      </div>

      <div class="lg:col-span-7" data-reveal="up" data-reveal-delay="1">
        <div class="grid grid-cols-12 gap-4 sm:gap-6">
          <div class="col-span-12 sm:col-span-7">
            <img
              src="{{ client.catering.image }}"
              alt="{{ client.catering.imageAlt or '' }}"
              loading="lazy"
              decoding="async"
              sizes="(min-width: 1024px) 32vw, (min-width: 640px) 40vw, 100vw"
              class="aspect-[4/5] w-full rounded-img object-cover shadow-card"
            />
          </div>
          {% if client.catering.secondImage %}
          <div class="col-span-12 sm:col-span-5 sm:mt-14 lg:mt-20">
            <img
              src="{{ client.catering.secondImage }}"
              alt="{{ client.catering.secondImageAlt or '' }}"
              loading="lazy"
              decoding="async"
              sizes="(min-width: 1024px) 23vw, (min-width: 640px) 29vw, 100vw"
              class="aspect-[4/5] w-full rounded-img object-cover shadow-card"
            />
          </div>
          {% endif %}
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>
